# Not by Accident — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` for local development (`.env` is gitignored —
# never commit real values). In production (Vercel), set the same names
# under Project → Settings → Environment Variables instead of committing a
# file.
#
# Every variable prefixed VITE_ is bundled into the browser build and is
# therefore PUBLIC — anyone can read it from the shipped JavaScript. Only
# put values here that are safe to be public (the same is already true of
# Supabase's "anon" key by design: it has no power beyond what Row Level
# Security allows it).
#
# NEVER put the Supabase service-role key, or any other server-only secret,
# in a VITE_ variable or anywhere in this frontend project. This app has no
# server component of its own — if you later need service-role access (for
# example, a scheduled job that auto-publishes scheduled content), do it in
# a Supabase Edge Function (see supabase/functions/), which reads
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY from Supabase's own function environment, not
# from this file.

# Supabase project URL — Dashboard → Project Settings → API → Project URL
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://nfpvygufottgzdbthgwt.supabase.co

# Supabase anon/public key — Dashboard → Project Settings → API → anon public
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
